  "evicted": {
   "text": "IN THE WORLD OF TECHNOLOGY, THE USE OF CAPITAL LETTERS IS A COMMON PRACTICE FOR KEYWORDS, NAMES, AND IMPORTANT TERMS. FOR EXAMPLE, IN PROGRAMMING LANGUAGES, KEYWORDS ARE WRITTEN IN ALL CAPS TO DISTINGUISH THEM FROM OTHER TEXT. THIS STYLE IS ALSO USED IN DOCUMENTATION, USER INTERFACES, AND CERTIFICATION CERTIFICATES.\n\nTHE USE OF CAPITAL LETTERS CAN HAVE MULTIPLE MEANINGS DEPENDING ON THE CONTEXT. IN SOME CASES, IT IS USED TO EMPHASIZE A WORD OR TO INDICATE A SPECIFIC TERM. IN OTHERS, IT MAY BE A STYLE CHOICE TO MAKE THE TEXT MORE READABLE OR TO FOLLOW A PARTICULAR DOCUMENTATION STYLE.\n\nIT IS IMPORTANT TO USE CAPITAL LETTERS RESPONSIBLY. WHILE IT CAN BE A GOOD IDEA TO USE THEM FOR KEYWORDS OR NAMES, IT IS NOT ALWAYS RECOMMENDED TO USE THEM FOR EVERY WORD. OVERUSE CAN MAKE THE TEXT APPEAR UNREADABLE OR UNprofessional.\n\nIN SUMMARY, THE USE OF CAPITAL LETTERS IS A TOOL THAT CAN BE USED EFFECTIVELY IN MANY CONTEXTS, BUT IT IS NOT A UNIVERSAL SOLUTION. THE KEY IS TO USE IT IN A WAY THAT MEETS THE NEEDS OF THE DOCUMENT OR THE USER.",
